{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '54,78p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md; sed -n '60,160p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md\"","aggregated_output":"| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| MC01 | Account for complete annual, quarterly and semi-annual disclosure packages, including notes and relevant referenced material. U1, U3. | Define the source inventory, coverage units, cross-reference closure and disposition rules. A worked filing package must account for retained, structured, duplicated and unresolved content without treating page extraction as semantic completion. | Specified procedure; acquired-file inventory checked. Ch. 2 Apple and Ch. 3 coverage; `cases/apple/manifest.json` accounts for 121 annual pages, 13 annual notes and 10 interim notes. External incorporated documents and full semantic translation remain incomplete. G5, G11. The added source corpus now has 192 checked annual/interim files across nine issuers and 2018–2025; incorporated-package closure and semantic annotation remain open. |\n| MC02 | Preserve numeric meaning: entities, perimeter, concept, dimensions, currency, units, scale, sign, basis and precision. U1, D. | Complete context/value types and compatibility rules, with valid/invalid examples and faithful rendering of the original disclosed amounts. | Specified in Chs. 3, 7 and Core 0 Context/Domain/Posting records, including display and rounding metadata. Schema, source scales and rounded-debt calculations have bounded checks; bounded debt context/type/source-binding checks and schema-valid rejection cases now pass. General context/type validation remains incomplete. G2, G3, G12. |\n| MC03 | Represent narrative policies, qualifications, commitments and cross-references, including material that is not executable yet. U1, U3, D. | Specify narrative assertion types, modality/quantifiers, links to affected amounts and obligations, and reviewed translation into constraints without inventing thresholds. | Specified Narrative/coverage records and modality rules in Ch. 3 and Core 0. Apple note and cross-reference obligations are retained; representative debt language is interpreted. Complete translation of all material narratives remains open. G2, G11. |\n| MC04 | Separate reported assertions, extraction readings, derivations, assumptions and conflicts. U1, U2, P, D. | Define source/derived/assumed status propagation and conflict handling; show both extraction error and a genuinely conflicting disclosure without silently changing either source. | Specified source/assumption constraints, review actions and conflict sets in Chs. 3, 6, 10. The 720-to-120 OCR repair differs from the 120-to-110 reported correction; transitive invalidation has a reference check. Bounded debt acceptance/source/assumption links are now checked; full workflow validation remains pending. G2, G15, G17. |\n| MC05 | Represent economic, reporting, publication/availability and system times; preserve original and revised history. U1, U3, D. | Specify original, latest-available and harmonised queries, cutoffs, supersession, calendar/interval rules and retrospective/prospective changes. Include exact annual/interim/restatement fixtures. | Specified in Chs. 2–3 and EvidenceView/Time contracts. Four publication/ingestion queries and compatible annual-minus-interim subtraction are reference-checked in `temporal.json`. Debt dates, periods, publication/ingestion/review cutoffs now have semantic rejection checks. General calendar and standards-transition implementations remain pending. G2, G4, G13. The accepted corpus records sourced filing dates for 56 reports and explicitly unverified publication dates for 136; as-of forecasting remains blocked where availability is unknown. |\n| MC06 | Distinguish legal entities, ownership, control, group perimeter and consolidation. U1, D. | Provide dated entity/control and adjustment-book types, acquisition/disposal and intragroup examples, and rules preventing unexplained consolidation plugs. | Specified structural control/elimination model; Ch. 9 and `sectors.json` check a simplified 80% acquisition, intragroup loan and full disposal. Actual control conclusions, goodwill/tax/FX and complex retained interests need further authority and operations. G4, G7, G12. |\n| MC07 | Align differing company labels and overlapping dimensions without equating unlike measurements or double counting. U1, D. | Specify concept/mapping relationships, applicability and aggregation rules; demonstrate company extensions and product/geography totals over the same population. | Specified mapping composition, applicability and partition obligations in Ch. 3/Core 0. The product/channel overlap counterexample is checked; general company-extension/mapping validation awaits implementation. G2, G12. |\n\n## M2 — Histories, interpretation and uncertainty\n\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| MC08 | Preserve jointly consistent discrete alternatives and continuous unknowns across accounts, notes and dates. U2, D. | Define history-family and choice/constraint semantics; provide cases preserving linked alternatives and rejecting incompatible combinations without independent account-by-account selection. | Specified shared symbols, choices and joint formulas in Chs. 2, 6–8. Exact reference checks retain fixed/floating histories, reject incompatible debt and reject incompatible marginal extrema. General reconstruction implementation remains pending. G1, G2, G15. |\n| MC09 | Construct historical families through a specified method, with honest scope and search completeness. U2, U3, D. | Define candidate templates, model-scope records, instantiation and constraint lowering, feasible/infeasible/unknown results, truncation and coverage evidence. | Specified finite template/slot construction and coverage rules in Ch. 6/Core 0. Northstar bridges are solved and checked within the declared scope; completeness concerns that model only. A compiler for arbitrary supported template registries remains pending. G1, G3. |\n| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\n| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\n\n## M3 — Economic events, journals and forecasts\n\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| MC13 | Drive economic events from contract state and explicit behaviour, then apply accounting rules and atomic journal/state updates. U2, D. | Specify one reference economic model, event payloads, recognition/measurement operations, preconditions, ordering and atomic transitions. Prove the stated bookkeeping invariant and separately define admissibility. | Specified Northstar economic decisions, event preconditions and operations in Chs. 2, 8. Reference journals, atomic rejection and idempotency checks pass. This verifies the bounded oracle, not a production event engine or accounting compliance. G2, G4, G6. |\n| MC14 | Give scenarios and decision information explicit meanings. U2, P, D. | Define supported exogenous stress, observational-conditioning and intervention modes, or explicitly scope unsupported modes; enforce information dates and distinguish real-world from pricing measures. | Specified exogenous stress, observational conditioning, intervention preconditions and information capabilities in Ch. 8/Core 0. Finite conditioning, an information-date example and debt stress typing/provenance are checked; causal intervention execution and arbitrary information-policy enforcement remain pending. G6, G14. |\n### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\n\nRequirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\nEvidence: [concept relationships](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:54)\nand [contextual aggregation](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:69).\n\nEquivalent, component, broader, reclassified and measurement-transformed\nconcepts are named, and partitions are required. Their records, applicability\nconditions and allowed compositions are not fully defined. There is no worked\ncase showing company extensions changing over time, gross/net distinctions,\nor two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\n\nRequired evidence: a mapping registry and application rules, with cases where\nsimilar labels mean different measurements and different labels mean the same\nquantity. Define what proves a partition disjoint/exhaustive, how unallocated\nresiduals are represented and how perimeter/context changes affect mappings.\nThe representation need not impose one universal chart of accounts, but it\nmust specify how comparability is established or left unresolved.\n\n### G13. Multiple clocks are identified without complete historical query rules\n\nRequirements: MC05, MC19, MC25. Refines G2, G4 and G10.\nEvidence: [time and views](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:80)\nand [EvidenceView](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:92).\n\nStoring dates and supersession links does not specify which assertion wins a\nquery. The design needs precise rules for incomplete publication timestamps,\nconflicting available filings, selective restatements, changed accounting\nbases and calendars, and different investor-information versus system-version\nqueries. Prospective estimate changes and retrospective corrections are\ndelegated to future packages without a complete transition example.\n\nRequired evidence: a multi-date example with explicit publication, ingestion,\neconomic and reporting times, original and revised amounts, and the exact\nrecords/results returned by each supported view. Show invalid year-to-date\nsubtractions across revisions as well as a valid one. Declare unsupported\ntiming assumptions rather than silently using the latest available row.\n\n### G14. Scenario modes and permitted information need enforceable contracts\n\nRequirements: MC14, MC18. Refines G6 and crosses modelling/execution requirements.\nEvidence: [three scenario meanings](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/03-literature.tex:149),\n[information timing](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:121),\nand [scenario grammar](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/11-contracts.tex:51).\n\nThe literature chapter promises to distinguish an imposed exogenous path,\nan observational conditional forecast and an intervention. The surface example\nonly sets a driver. The record/API specification does not supply complete\nmode-specific semantics for conditioning or replacing equations. Similarly,\nbehavioural and measurement plugins are told to use permissible information,\nbut the available-information object and its access rules are unspecified.\n\nRequired evidence: declare supported scenario kinds and represent them in the\nschema. A first release can explicitly support exogenous stress only without\nclaiming the other operations. Show how a manager and an allowance calculation\nreceive current information while future simulated outcomes remain hidden.\nExplain when new observed evidence updates historical weights and why merely\nselecting a hypothetical stress does not do so.\n\n### G15. Different kinds of uncertainty need different admissibility rules\n\nRequirements: MC04, MC08, MC10, MC12, MC24. Refines G1, G2 and G6.\nEvidence: [interpretation distinction](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/01-purpose.tex:67)\nand [alternative records](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:183).\n\nAn unknown fixed-rate share, two readings of a note, a permitted accounting\nelection, a measurement estimate and a future management decision are different\nuncertainties. The text recognises this, but generic symbols/choices and\nassumption provenance do not fully specify how each kind is validated,\nupdated or propagated. An unsupported treatment must not be accepted as an\nequally legitimate interpretation merely because it produces balanced entries.\n\nRequired evidence: define these distinctions in the model and review contracts,\nincluding links between dependent uncertainties. Show an admissible alternative,\nan evidence-refuted alternative and an unsupported accounting treatment.\nPreserve a possibly erroneous source assertion as evidence without silently\nendorsing its treatment. This requires no new fraud-detection product.\n\n### G16. Aggregation and history compression need a practical resolution policy\n\nRequirements: MC11, MC22. Refines G1 and G6.\nEvidence: [conditional-law equivalence](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/05-mathematics.tex:222).\n\nThe definition that grouped histories must have the same relevant conditional\nlaws is useful. It does not supply a usable rule for choosing instrument,\nlot, vintage or cohort resolution, carrying necessary accounting memory, or\nreconsidering a grouping when a scenario/horizon changes. The draft correctly\navoids claiming a general equivalence-deciding compiler, but does not specify\nenough supported transformations in its place.\n\nRequired evidence: define resolution metadata, state requirements and a small\nset of justified transformations. Include one grouping that preserves the\nrequested results and another that loses a rate, maturity or guarantee\nexposure. Declare the scope/error of approximate aggregation and retain its\nsource/detail references. Changing the query must trigger a sufficiency check.\n\n### G17. Local evidence review needs a state machine and invalidation rules\n\nRequirements: MC04, MC27. Refines G2, G5 and G10.\nEvidence: [review actions](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/09-implementation.tex:142)\nand [correction proposals](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/07-execution.tex:13).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
