{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'Original|LatestAvailable|Harmonised|supersess|YTD|date.only|ExtractionReading|HistoricalFact|FutureInnovation|BehaviourPolicy|MeasurementEstimate|AccountingElection|resolution|group|partition' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md docs/design/spec/reconstruction-profile-v1.md scripts/core_semantics.py scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\"","aggregated_output":"scripts/reconstruction_v1.py:12:    'ExtractionReading': ('source', 'locator', 'review_decision'),\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:13:    'HistoricalFact': ('evidence', 'reason'),\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:14:    'AccountingElection': ('package', 'permitted_treatments', 'election', 'effective_date', 'eligibility_evidence'),\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:15:    'MeasurementEstimate': ('method', 'measurement_date', 'inputs'),\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:16:    'BehaviourPolicy': ('policy', 'information_set', 'decision_time'),\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:17:    'FutureInnovation': ('driver', 'future_period', 'scenario', 'joint_law', 'measure'),\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:30:    if kind == 'ExtractionReading' and record['review_decision'] != 'Accept':\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:32:    if kind == 'AccountingElection' and record['election'] not in record['permitted_treatments']:\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:221:            if view['choice_group'] is not None:raise UnsupportedFragment('P03 choice group requires explicit partition')\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:286:def group_contracts(contracts, scenario, horizon, previous=None):\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:287:    \"\"\"Exact additive simple-debt grouping; retain full constituent memory.\"\"\"\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:290:    if previous and previous['signature']!=signature:raise ValueError('grouping requires revalidation')\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:291:    if not contracts or horizon[0]>=horizon[1]:raise ValueError('invalid grouping request')\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:308:    grouped=principal*rate*year_fraction\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:309:    if individual!=grouped:raise ValueError('additivity check failed')\nscripts/reconstruction_v1.py:312:            'interest':str(grouped),'transition_preserved':True,'report_preserved':True}\ndocs/design/spec/reconstruction-profile-v1.md:41:| grouping | explicit additive debt profile only | retain contract memory | different resets/maturities/horizon; revalidation tests |\ndocs/design/spec/reconstruction-profile-v1.md:51:are split by an exhaustive truth-assignment partition of their atomic comparisons;\ndocs/design/spec/reconstruction-profile-v1.md:52:each cell includes the formula and its decision prefix. The partition is disjoint\ndocs/design/spec/reconstruction-profile-v1.md:56:logical partition. Continuous regions remain symbolic. Unvisited suffixes are\nscripts/core_semantics.py:353:            require(s['uncertainty_kind'] == 'HistoricalFact' and r['action'] == 'Accept', 'UnsupportedAdmission', s['id'], 'This profile handles an admitted factual unknown')\nscripts/core_semantics.py:384:            require(a['choice_group'] is None, 'UnsupportedChoice', a['id'], 'Named conditional views only')\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:68:semantic checker validate these specific bindings; general registry resolution\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:118:dimension only through a valid partition mapping. Reference fields and source\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:159:timing/calendar resolution, allowed choices, bounds, and forbidden/unsupported\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:200:supersession removes only the targeted assertions in the same context. A\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:202:the acyclic supersession graph. Competing maximal assertions form a conflict\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:203:set, never a last-row-wins result. Original view chooses initial assertions in\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:210:end, units/basis/perimeter and revision group, or an explicit compatibility\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:219:Several accepted alternatives need a choice group. Reject never deletes source\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:221:accepted reading requires a supersession action. An unresolved contradiction\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:229:Uncertainty kinds are ExtractionReading, HistoricalFact, AccountingElection,\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:230:MeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy and FutureInnovation. Each has scope,\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:283:hashes normalised IR, assumptions, rule/calculator locks and resolution contract,\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:297:coupling-group, entity, contract/cohort, economic-date, shock-kind, draw-index),\ndocs/design/spec/core-contract.md:299:rational (integer+1/2)/2^64. Branch enumeration order is absent. Coupling groups\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '92,126p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '184,247p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '286,319p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py; cat docs/design/fixtures/temporal.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '92,126p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '184,247p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md; sed -n '286,319p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py; cat docs/design/fixtures/temporal.json\"","aggregated_output":"constraints. Choice members resolve within their choice namespace. The\nsurface syntax has no unbounded loops, recursion, dynamic code evaluation or\nhost calls; finite schedules/collections come from typed packages. Report\nfields bind supported mapping expressions and cannot override recognition.\nEvery assumption constraint or conditional model input has an Assumption\nrecord carrying its expression, scope, rationale, origin, evidence, validity\nperiod, information cutoff and role (Baseline, Hypothesis, Convenience or\nReviewedDefault). An authored baseline is not automatically a reviewed\ndefault. Conditional example endpoints are hypotheses, not inferred facts.\nThe debt example also records its assumed initial 5% component rates and 7%\nstress driver as assumptions. The integer contract-slot limit has its own\n`Int` literal; it does not reuse the `Real` literal in the fraction comparison.\n\n## Exact values, contexts and built-ins\n\nRationals use base-10 signed numerator strings and positive denominator strings,\nlowest terms; zero is `0/1`. Money adds only within one currency and compatible\ncontext. Real times money is money; rate times money must also supply a\nYearFraction through `simpleInterest`. Rate alone is not a dimensionless Real.\nNo rate basis is implicitly coerced. The demonstration's accrual rule uses\n`simpleInterest(principal,rate,fraction)` explicitly. Integer counts stay integer.\nDivision by a symbolic value\nrequires nonzero proof and is outside the rational-linear solver fragment.\n\nContext equality compares entity, perimeter version, measurement basis,\ncurrency/unit, instant/period/calendar and dimensions. A sum may discard a\ndimension only through a valid partition mapping. Reference fields and source\nspans may differ without changing financial comparability. Observation\nprecision is a domain, not a tolerance argument. Unknown rounding convention\nis an unresolved reading, not an assumed half-unit interval.\n\nDomain `display` preserves the disclosed spelling, unit/scale and sign when\navailable; `rounding_rule` identifies the declared convention or is null for\nan unrounded mathematical symbol. The SourceSpan retains the original text.\nAn exact numeric domain has equal closed bounds; an interval has ordered bounds\nFixed proportions times known totals are linear; variable F,V with F+V=D is\nlinear even when D is rounded. A fixed constraint F/D >= a with known a and\nproved D>0 becomes F>=aD; an unknown a restores bilinearity.\n\nFeasibility results are sat+exact witness, unsat+constraint/source core or\nunknown+reason+undecided formula. Bounds include lower/upper rational value,\nattainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\ninequalities require infimum/supremum semantics. An unbounded result is neither\nunknown nor a finite extreme. Resource budgets are explicit request fields;\ntimeout preserves undecided cells rather than deleting them.\n\n## Temporal selection and local review\n\nAn EvidenceView first filters by availability cutoff and (if requested)\ningestion cutoff. Day-only availability maps to the next local midnight using\nthe named timezone; finer availability requires evidence. Selective explicit\nsupersession removes only the targeted assertions in the same context. A\nsuperseding assertion must be eligible itself. Transitive successors follow\nthe acyclic supersession graph. Competing maximal assertions form a conflict\nset, never a last-row-wins result. Original view chooses initial assertions in\neach chain from a declared filing, not arbitrary earliest ingestion. A filing\nwith no prior version supplies its original itself. Harmonisation derives new\nobservations, preserves originals and records all transformation rules.\n\nIntervals are [start,end_exclusive) in a calendar; balance instants refer to\nthe end-of-day boundary. Cumulative subtraction requires same start, nested\nend, units/basis/perimeter and revision group, or an explicit compatibility\nassertion supported by review. A restatement of one flow does not restate every\nnote. Prospective estimate changes affect events from their effective date;\nretrospective corrections generate a new view and an explicit opening bridge.\n\nReview states are Proposed, Accepted, AcceptedAlternative, Rejected and\nSuperseded. Accept requires verified locator/literal, context, rationale,\nreviewer/date, applicability checks and a reconciliation result. Acceptance\nof an extraction is separate from acceptance of an accounting interpretation.\nSeveral accepted alternatives need a choice group. Reject never deletes source\nbytes. Correction creates a new reading linked to the old one; replacing an\naccepted reading requires a supersession action. An unresolved contradiction\nsets conflict, even if each extraction was accepted. No LLM confidence becomes\na hypothesis weight. Derived formulas, mappings, measurements and runs record\ndependency IDs; a changed decision makes their descendants stale for new\nviews. Historic frozen runs remain replayable, labelled with their old view.\n\n## Uncertainty, scenarios and results\n\nUncertainty kinds are ExtractionReading, HistoricalFact, AccountingElection,\nMeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy and FutureInnovation. Each has scope,\ndomain, evidence, dependencies and admission rule. An election needs a dated\npermitted treatment and evidence of eligibility; a balanced but prohibited\ntreatment is UnsupportedTreatment. Estimates need a method/date/inputs; future\ninnovations need a joint law and measure. New observations constrain facts;\ncorrections replace evidence views; likelihoods update probability models;\nhypothetical stresses alone do none of those.\n\nExogenousStress supplies named driver paths without updating historical weights.\nObservationalConditioning supplies observed events, a joint model and positive\nevent probability/likelihood; finite enumeration computes normalised joint\nweights exactly. Zero probability yields UndefinedConditioning, not equal\nweights. Continuous density conditioning requires an explicit conditional\nmodel/regular conditional distribution adapter. StructuralIntervention replaces\nspecified equations in a named acyclic structural model, retaining exogenous\nnoise; absence of that model yields UnsupportedScenario. Risk-neutral pricing\nand real-world simulation measures have different IDs and cannot be mixed\nwithout an explicit justified transformation.\ndef group_contracts(contracts, scenario, horizon, previous=None):\n    \"\"\"Exact additive simple-debt grouping; retain full constituent memory.\"\"\"\n    request={'contracts':contracts,'scenario':scenario,'horizon':horizon}\n    signature=hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(request,sort_keys=True).encode()).hexdigest()\n    if previous and previous['signature']!=signature:raise ValueError('grouping requires revalidation')\n    if not contracts or horizon[0]>=horizon[1]:raise ValueError('invalid grouping request')\n    if len({c['id'] for c in contracts}) != len(contracts):\n        raise ValueError('duplicate contract identity would double-count principal')\n    allowed = {'id', 'principal', 'rate', 'reset', 'maturity', 'hedge'}\n    if any(set(c) != allowed or c['hedge'] != 'none' or c['reset'] not in ('fixed','floating')\n           or rational(c['principal']) < 0 for c in contracts):\n        raise UnsupportedFragment('only nonnegative unhedged bullet debt is supported')\n    keys=('rate','reset','maturity','hedge')\n    if any(tuple(c[k] for k in keys)!=tuple(contracts[0][k] for k in keys) for c in contracts):\n        raise UnsupportedFragment('different contract memory keys')\n    if any(c['maturity']<=horizon[1] for c in contracts):raise UnsupportedFragment('maturity inside horizon')\n    rate=rational(scenario['rate'] if contracts[0]['reset']=='floating' else contracts[0]['rate'])\n    year_fraction=rational(scenario['year_fraction'])\n    if year_fraction <= 0:\n        raise ValueError('positive declared horizon year fraction required')\n    principal=sum((rational(c['principal']) for c in contracts),F(0))\n    individual=sum((rational(c['principal'])*rate*year_fraction for c in contracts),F(0))\n    grouped=principal*rate*year_fraction\n    if individual!=grouped:raise ValueError('additivity check failed')\n    return {'signature':signature,'status':'ExactForDeclaredAdditiveProfile','memory':deepcopy(contracts),\n            'scenario':deepcopy(scenario),'horizon':list(horizon),'principal':str(principal),\n            'interest':str(grouped),'transition_preserved':True,'report_preserved':True}\n{\n  \"availability_policy\": \"date-only filing is available at next midnight in stated reporting timezone\",\n  \"assertions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"h1-original\",\n      \"key\": \"revenue:H1:USD:NS:Demo\",\n      \"value\": \"120\",\n      \"available\": \"2024-08-01T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"ingested\": \"2024-08-03T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"vintage\": \"v1\",\n      \"supersedes\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"h1-restated\",\n      \"key\": \"revenue:H1:USD:NS:Demo\",\n      \"value\": \"110\",\n      \"available\": \"2025-03-02T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"ingested\": \"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"vintage\": \"v2\",\n      \"supersedes\": [\n        \"h1-original\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fy\",\n      \"key\": \"revenue:FY:USD:NS:Demo\",\n      \"value\": \"260\",\n      \"available\": \"2025-03-02T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"ingested\": \"2025-03-05T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"vintage\": \"v2\",\n      \"supersedes\": []\n    }\n  ],\n  \"queries\": [\n    {\n      \"cutoff\": \"2024-09-01T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"system_as_of\": null,\n      \"expect\": [\n        \"h1-original\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"cutoff\": \"2025-03-03T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"system_as_of\": null,\n      \"expect\": [\n        \"h1-restated\",\n        \"fy\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"cutoff\": \"2025-03-03T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"system_as_of\": \"2025-03-04T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"expect\": [\n        \"h1-original\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"cutoff\": \"2025-03-06T00:00:00Z\",\n      \"system_as_of\": null,\n      \"mode\": \"original\",\n      \"expect\": [\n        \"h1-original\",\n        \"fy\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"expected_valid_h2\": \"150\",\n  \"incompatible_vintage_h2\": \"140 must be rejected\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,115p' scripts/check_accounting_p04.py; rg -n 'approved.plan|execution.inventory|entry_inventory|inventory_path|worker_limit|P06' scripts/run_accounting_master.py scripts/accounting_master_support.py scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json; sed -n '1,48p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,115p' scripts/check_accounting_p04.py; rg -n 'approved.plan|execution.inventory|entry_inventory|inventory_path|worker_limit|P06' scripts/run_accounting_master.py scripts/accounting_master_support.py scripts/accounting_master_catalog.json; sed -n '1,48p' scripts/reconstruction_v1.py\"","aggregated_output":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Execute P04 obligations, regress P03, and retain supervisor inventory evidence.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom datetime import datetime, timezone\nimport hashlib\nimport io\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport platform\nimport re\nimport shlex\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport unittest\nimport z3\nfrom check_accounting_p03 import capture_protection, finish_protection, digest, _inventory, _unique_object\nROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nHISTORICAL_INVENTORY='data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/phase-entry-inventory.json'\nORIGINAL_PLAN='data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T221346-d54a6552/P04/approved-plan.json'\nSOURCES=['scripts/rational_solver_v1.py','scripts/reconstruction_v1.py','scripts/check_accounting_p04.py','tests/test_accounting_p04.py','docs/design/spec/reconstruction-profile-v1.md','docs/design/fixtures/p04-reconstruction-cases-v1.json']\nOUTPUTS=['data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04/'+p for p in ('conformance.json','result.md','progress.md')]\n\ndef repository_path(root, relative):\n    path=Path(relative)\n    if (path.is_absolute() or '..' in path.parts or path.as_posix()!=relative\n            or not (root/path).resolve().is_relative_to(root.resolve())):\n        raise ValueError('provenance path must be repository-relative and remain inside the repository')\n    return path\n\n\ndef approval_reference(root, relative):\n    path=repository_path(root,relative)\n    raw=(root/path).read_bytes()\n    record=json.loads(raw,object_pairs_hook=_unique_object)\n    if not isinstance(record,dict):\n        raise ValueError('approval must be an object')\n    for name,verdict in (('plan','PLAN'),('review','AGREE')):\n        response=record.get(name)\n        if not isinstance(response,dict) or response.get('verdict')!=verdict:\n            raise ValueError('approval requires a PLAN and an AGREE review')\n        if not isinstance(response.get('summary'),str):\n            raise ValueError('malformed approval summary')\n        for key in ('steps','assumptions','checks','evidence','issues','residuals','next_actions'):\n            if not isinstance(response.get(key),list) or not all(isinstance(x,str) for x in response[key]):\n                raise ValueError('malformed approval '+key)\n    if record['review']['issues']:\n        raise ValueError('no issue-free approved plan')\n    plan_hash=hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(record['plan'],sort_keys=True,ensure_ascii=False,\n                                      separators=(',',':'),allow_nan=False).encode()).hexdigest()\n    if record.get('plan_hash')!=plan_hash:\n        raise ValueError('approved plan hash mismatch')\n    return {'path':relative,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest(),'plan_hash':plan_hash}\n\n\ndef prepare_provenance(root, execution_inventory, approved_plan):\n    execution=repository_path(root,execution_inventory)\n    plan=repository_path(root,approved_plan)\n    if (plan.name!='approved-plan.json' or plan.parent.name!='P04'\n            or plan.parent.parent.parent!=Path('data/accounting-master/runs')\n            or execution.name!='pre-edit-files.json'\n            or not re.fullmatch(r'execution-\\d+',execution.parent.name)\n            or execution.parent.parent!=plan.parent):\n        raise ValueError('use a supervisor P04 approval and execution inventory from the same run')\n    references={'approved_plan':approval_reference(root,approved_plan),\n                'original_design':approval_reference(root,ORIGINAL_PLAN)}\n    execution_baseline=_inventory(root,execution_inventory)\n    protected=capture_protection(root,HISTORICAL_INVENTORY,execution_inventory,writable=SOURCES+OUTPUTS,\n                                 required_paths=('docs/design/fixtures/borrowings.json','docs/design/fixtures/northstar.json','scripts/core0_ir_v1.py'))\n    if protected['errors'] or protected['changed_since_execution_entry'] or protected['missing_before_check']:\n        raise ValueError('protection failure before execution: '+str(protected['errors']+protected['changed_since_execution_entry']))\n    for label,path in (('historical_inventory',HISTORICAL_INVENTORY),('execution_inventory',execution_inventory)):\n        references[label]={'path':path,'sha256':protected['inventory_hashes'][path]}\n    return protected,references,execution_baseline\n\n\ndef execute_checks():\n    sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'tests'))\n    import test_accounting_p04 as p04\n    import test_accounting_p03 as p03\n    p04.OBSERVATIONS.clear();p03.OBSERVATIONS.clear()\n    reports={}\n    for name,module in [('P04',p04),('P03_regression',p03)]:\n        stream=io.StringIO();suite=unittest.defaultTestLoader.loadTestsFromModule(module)\n        result=unittest.TextTestRunner(stream=stream,verbosity=2).run(suite)\n        reports[name]={'methods':result.testsRun,'failures':len(result.failures),'errors':len(result.errors),\n                       'skips':len(result.skipped),'passed':result.wasSuccessful() and result.testsRun>0 and not result.skipped,'output':stream.getvalue()}\n    catalog=json.loads((ROOT/SOURCES[-1]).read_text())\n    required=Counter(x['id'] for x in catalog['obligations']);observed=Counter(x['obligation'] for x in p04.OBSERVATIONS)\n    status={'required':len(required),'observed':len(observed),'missing':sorted(required.keys()-observed.keys()),\n            'uncatalogued':sorted(observed.keys()-required.keys()),\n            'duplicate_ids':sorted(k for k in required.keys()|observed.keys() if required[k]>1 or observed[k]>1),\n            'failed_observations':[x['obligation'] for x in p04.OBSERVATIONS if x.get('passed') is not True]}\n    return reports,list(p04.OBSERVATIONS),status,catalog\n\n\ndef main(argv=None):\n    parser=argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    parser.add_argument('--output-dir',required=True)\n    parser.add_argument('--execution-inventory',required=True)\n    parser.add_argument('--approved-plan',required=True)\n    args=parser.parse_args(argv)\n    if Path(args.output_dir).resolve()!=ROOT/'data/accounting-master/deliverables/P04':\n        parser.error('use the declared P04 output directory')\n    started=time.monotonic();utc=datetime.now(timezone.utc).isoformat()\n    try:\n        protected,references,execution_baseline=prepare_provenance(ROOT,args.execution_inventory,args.approved_plan)\n    except (OSError,ValueError) as exc:\n        parser.error(str(exc))\n    os.environ['CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES']='-1'\n    source_before={p:digest(ROOT/p) for p in SOURCES}\n    source_before.update({r['path']:r['sha256'] for r in references.values()})\n    reports,observations,status,catalog=execute_checks()\n    finish_protection(ROOT,protected)\nscripts/accounting_master_catalog.json:213:      \"id\": \"P06\",\nscripts/accounting_master_catalog.json:248:      \"output_dir\": \"data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06\"\nscripts/accounting_master_catalog.json:256:        \"P06\"\nscripts/accounting_master_catalog.json:418:        \"P06\",\nscripts/accounting_master_catalog.json:451:        \"P06\",\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:155:        for field in ['entry_inventory_path', 'accepted_at', 'block_signature']:\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:632:        budget = {'worker_limit_seconds': seconds, 'available_attempt_seconds': round(available, 1),\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:741:            'Planning must stay bounded: use a few grouped targeted reads of relevant existing inputs/interfaces, then return the executable plan. Do not perform the entire accounting analysis or implementation during planning. On recovery, use the prior approved plan and current partial work to plan the remaining repairs under every original criterion. Do not restart discovery. Keep the final plan under 1800 words.',\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:954:            if record.get('entry_inventory_path') and 'contributed_files' not in record:\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:966:            atomic_json(folder / 'approved-plan.json', {**fixed_plan, 'plan_hash': stable_hash(fixed_plan)})\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1003:                atomic_json(folder / 'approved-plan.json', approved)\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1011:        if record.get('entry_inventory_path'):\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1012:            entry = load_json(local_path(self.root, record['entry_inventory_path']))\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1017:            record['entry_inventory_path'] = str(entry_path.relative_to(self.root))\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1019:        packet['phase_entry_inventory'] = record['entry_inventory_path']\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1022:            if stable_hash(load_json(folder / 'approved-plan.json')['plan']) != approved['plan_hash']:\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1035:                if stable_hash(load_json(folder / 'approved-plan.json')['plan']) != approved['plan_hash']:\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1036:                    raise ContinuationVeto('Implementation changed its approved plan')\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1054:                if stable_hash(load_json(folder / 'approved-plan.json')['plan']) != approved['plan_hash']:\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1055:                    raise ContinuationVeto('Result review changed the approved plan')\nscripts/run_accounting_master.py:1064:                    names.add(str((folder / 'approved-plan.json').relative_to(self.root)))\nscripts/accounting_master_support.py:401:    inventory = record.get('entry_inventory_path')\nscripts/accounting_master_support.py:411:        'entry_inventory_path': inventory,\nscripts/accounting_master_support.py:417:        'approved_plan': ['approved-plan.json'],\nscripts/accounting_master_support.py:446:            elif kind == 'approved_plan':\n\"\"\"Declared-template reconstruction and bounded uncertainty operations, version 1.\"\"\"\nfrom copy import deepcopy\nfrom fractions import Fraction as F\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nimport z3\nfrom rational_solver_v1 import (Problem, Budget, UnsupportedFragment, q, rational, domain_formula,\n                                disclosure_domain, half_even, solve)\n\n\nADMISSION_FIELDS = {\n    'ExtractionReading': ('source', 'locator', 'review_decision'),\n    'HistoricalFact': ('evidence', 'reason'),\n    'AccountingElection': ('package', 'permitted_treatments', 'election', 'effective_date', 'eligibility_evidence'),\n    'MeasurementEstimate': ('method', 'measurement_date', 'inputs'),\n    'BehaviourPolicy': ('policy', 'information_set', 'decision_time'),\n    'FutureInnovation': ('driver', 'future_period', 'scenario', 'joint_law', 'measure'),\n}\n\n\ndef admit(record):\n    kind = record.get('kind')\n    if kind not in ADMISSION_FIELDS:\n        raise ValueError('unknown uncertainty category')\n    for key in ('id', 'scope', 'provenance', 'dependencies') + ADMISSION_FIELDS[kind]:\n        if key not in record or (key != 'dependencies' and not record[key]):\n            raise ValueError('missing admission field: ' + key)\n    if not isinstance(record['dependencies'], list) or not isinstance(record['provenance'], list):\n        raise ValueError('dependencies and provenance must be explicit lists')\n    if kind == 'ExtractionReading' and record['review_decision'] != 'Accept':\n        raise ValueError('extraction reading is not accepted')\n    if kind == 'AccountingElection' and record['election'] not in record['permitted_treatments']:\n        raise ValueError('treatment not permitted by declared package')\n    return deepcopy(record)\n\n\ndef expression(node, env):\n    if isinstance(node, bool):\n        return z3.BoolVal(node)\n    if isinstance(node, (str, int, F)):\n        return env[node] if isinstance(node, str) and node in env else q(node)\n    if not isinstance(node, list) or not node:\n        raise ValueError('expression must be exact scalar, reference or operation list')\n    op, *args = node\n    args = [expression(x, env) for x in args]\n    ops = {'+': lambda a,b:a+b, '-': lambda a,b:a-b, '*': lambda a,b:a*b,\n           '/': lambda a,b:a/b, '==': lambda a,b:a==b, '<=': lambda a,b:a<=b,\n           '>=': lambda a,b:a>=b, '<': lambda a,b:a<b, '>': lambda a,b:a>b,\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '60,78p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '68,76p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md; sed -n '1,80p' docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md; rg -n '\"'^def |concept|merge_context'\"' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py | head -45\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '60,78p' docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md; sed -n '68,76p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md; sed -n '1,80p' docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md; rg -n '\"'^def |concept|merge_context'\"' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py | head -45\"","aggregated_output":"### G12. Cross-company concepts and aggregation need formal mapping semantics\n\nRequirements: MC02, MC06, MC07, MC20, MC24. Refines G2, G4 and G7.\nEvidence: [concept relationships](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/02-history.tex:54)\nand [contextual aggregation](/home/chakwong/python/AccDSL/docs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:69).\n\nEquivalent, component, broader, reclassified and measurement-transformed\nconcepts are named, and partitions are required. Their records, applicability\nconditions and allowed compositions are not fully defined. There is no worked\ncase showing company extensions changing over time, gross/net distinctions,\nor two classifications of the same revenue that must not be summed together.\n\nRequired evidence: a mapping registry and application rules, with cases where\nsimilar labels mean different measurements and different labels mean the same\nquantity. Define what proves a partition disjoint/exhaustive, how unallocated\nresiduals are represented and how perimeter/context changes affect mappings.\nThe representation need not impose one universal chart of accounts, but it\nmust specify how comparability is established or left unresolved.\n\n| MC09 | Construct historical families through a specified method, with honest scope and search completeness. U2, U3, D. | Define candidate templates, model-scope records, instantiation and constraint lowering, feasible/infeasible/unknown results, truncation and coverage evidence. | Specified finite template/slot construction and coverage rules in Ch. 6/Core 0. Northstar bridges are solved and checked within the declared scope; completeness concerns that model only. A compiler for arbitrary supported template registries remains pending. G1, G3. |\n| MC10 | Distinguish uncertainty about facts, disclosure readings, admissible accounting treatment, estimates, behaviour and future shocks. U2, P, D. | Specify the categories, dependencies and admissibility checks; show why a factual unknown, permitted election and unsupported treatment cannot be substituted for one another. | Specified six uncertainty kinds with separate admission/provenance/dependency rules in Core 0 and Chs. 6–8. Examples distinguish factual composition, permitted inventory election and unsupported treatment. Factual/assumption admission is now tested for the authored debt case; all-category semantic validation remains pending. G6, G15. |\n| MC11 | Preserve the economic memory and scenario responses needed when histories are aggregated or refined. U2, D. | Define required state by contract/lot/cohort, permitted grouping transformations, supported horizon/scenarios, exact versus approximate status and invalidation when the query changes. | Specified grouping keys, additive transition/report proof, exact/approximate status and query invalidation in Ch. 6/Core 0. Debt, lot and cohort counterexamples are given; a general equivalence checker or empirical approximate-cohort error bound is not established. G1, G16. |\n| MC12 | Add probabilities only under an explicit justified joint measure, and retain unweighted alternatives when weights are unsupported. U2, P, D. | Specify optional weight/prior/likelihood records, dependence, overlaps, updates and mass preservation; provide a worked weighted and unweighted example with clear interpretation. | Specified finite joint weighting and one-use likelihood update in Ch. 6/Core 0; exact posterior 3/11 and 8/11, mixture and retained unresolved mass are checked. Continuous inference requires a target-specific method and validation. G2, G6, G15. |\n\n## M3 — Economic events, journals and forecasts\n\n| ID | Requirement and origin | Evidence needed to complete the design | Current assessment and related gaps |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n# Core 0.1 debt source lowering, version 1\n\nThis executable profile supplements the protected Core 0 grammar and contract.\n`compile_source(text, bindings)` parses real source; `compile_program(Program,\nbindings)` accepts immutable typed declarations. Both bind names, check quantities\nand context, construct shared IR, and submit it to independent schema and semantic\nvalidation. Neither entrypoint reads the authored expected IR or expected results.\n\n## Execution evidence contract\n\nThe approved P03 plan remains the implementation boundary. Acceptance requires\nreal source lowering, independent typed/source equivalence, changed-input\nsensitivity, semantic rejection and complete catalog execution. The current\nimplementation preserves global constraints, explicit annual-rate units,\nacceptance records, package bindings and domain checks.\n\nThe baseline is `borrowing.acc`, plus documented corresponding fields of the\nauthored IR, whose reconstruction claims are excluded. Independently constructed\ntyped programs and exact arithmetic checks supplement agreement between frontends.\nSchema validity is a prerequisite, not semantic acceptance. Negative IR cases must\nbe structurally valid before testing the intended semantic rejection. Stops are\nunexpected protected-input changes, missing dependencies, or failing mandatory\nchecks; failures trigger repair, never a passing report. No statistical, timing,\nusability, accounting-compliance or forecasting comparison is being run.\n\nProvenance of material choices: exact rationals, lexical rules and quantities come\nfrom `core-contract.md`; USD accounts and DebtMix fields come from the local\nDemoDebt package. These are bounded baseline restrictions, not promoted defaults.\nThe single source/observation/symbol restriction keeps the evidence view explicit;\nmultiple-source reconciliation is unsupported. Synthetic acceptance and admission\nrecords are supplied by the caller. Absence of reconstruction requires Unknown\nfeasibility, PartialSearch, zero completed cells, one unsearched cell, no witnesses\nand no solver results. Early diagnostics cover unit loss, silent constraint loss,\ninvented acceptance and copied package digests. A pass establishes deterministic\nengineering conformance only. Results are preserved in the two P03 deliverables.\n\nThe writable project files are the two versioned modules, checker, required test,\nthis profile, the versioned cases JSON and the two P03 deliverables. Existing\ngrammar/schema, authored fixtures, legacy validators, controllers, release-pinned\nfiles and preserved snapshots remain protected. Recorded protected inputs are\nchecked against durable supervisor execution-entry hashes and before/after the\ncheck; historical phase-entry differences are separately attributed. Git is\nunavailable (existing marker is not a usable repository); no Git initialization.\nPython 3.11.15, Lark 1.3.1 and jsonschema 4.26.0 are existing dependencies. No\naccelerator framework, service, installation, model or background job is used.\n\n## Supported language and bindings\n\nThe profile has one module, DemoDebt@1 import, source, entity, USD book, exact\ninstant debt observation, admitted Real interval symbol, opening, DebtMix\ncontract, constant annual-rate stress and package report. Its four account names\nare Cash, Debt, InterestExpense and Retained, with Asset, Liability, Expense and\nEquity roles respectively: the package report actually names these accounts.\nOther declaration names may vary. There may be multiple lets, Boolean constraints\nand conditional alternatives, with multiple assumptions in each alternative.\nGlobal constraints constrain the parent family; alternative constraints stay in\ntheir respective branches and are not conjoined in the parent. No branch is\nselected or solved.\n\nBindings explicitly supply a digest-locked local package, synthetic reading and\nacceptance action, information/system cutoffs, opening balances, perimeter,\nsymbol admission, assumption periods/origins, and alternative authorship. Binding\nrecords remain separate from package definitions. Every acceptance must explicitly\nsay Accept; no declaration creates acceptance. Package loading is restricted to\nthe retained DemoDebt file and checks its fixed version, digest, exports and\napplicability. Paths escaping the repository and overrides are errors. The\npackage's registry examples and expected-result fields are not compiler inputs.\n\nDecimal tokens become Fraction directly; binary floats are rejected. Strings use\nJSON escapes, reject unpaired surrogates and normalize semantic strings to NFC.\nOriginal spelling and Unicode-code-point offsets remain in the separate source\nmap; typed locations identify constructors. LF, CRLF, comments and whitespace\npreserve semantics. Dates are Gregorian. All grammar words are reserved.\n\nExpressions include literals, shared references, `value(observation)`, unary minus,\n`not`, compatible addition/subtraction, numeric comparisons, typed equality and\nBoolean composition. Multiplication admits a dimensionless Real or Int factor;\ndivision requires a provably nonzero constant Real or Int denominator. Rates and\nYearFraction are dimensional; rate times money is rejected here (the general\n`simpleInterest` builtin is future work). Integer products remain integer; division\n99:def _pairs(value: Mapping[str, Any] | Iterable[tuple[str, Any]] | None) -> tuple[tuple[str, Any], ...]:\n107:def _tuple(value: Iterable[Any] | None) -> tuple[Any, ...]:\n111:def _fraction(value: Fraction | int | str | Decimal) -> Fraction:\n126:def rational(value: Fraction | int | str | Decimal) -> dict[str, str]:\n131:def parse_rational(value: Mapping[str, str]) -> Fraction:\n144:def _clean_id(value: str) -> str:\n149:def _iso(value: str, where: str) -> str:\n159:def _string(value: str) -> str:\n165:def binding_projection(value: Any) -> Any:\n180:def _instant(value: str, where: str) -> str:\n190:def _time(kind: str, start: str, end: Optional[str], calendar: str) -> dict[str, Any]:\n686:def _unique(rows, attr, key, code):\n693:def _validate_bindings(bindings: CompileBindings) -> None:\n823:def _empty_ir() -> dict[str, Any]:\n838:def _diag(code: str, message: str, location: str, capability: Optional[str] = None,\n1144:            context = _merge_context(left[2], right[2], owner, self)\n1298:                                         \"role\": account.role, \"report_concept\": account.name})\n1323:                \"concept\": \"debt_principal\", \"basis\": package.id, \"measurement\": \"principal\",\n1528:def _numeric_type(typ: str) -> bool:\n1532:def _is_scalar(typ: str) -> bool:\n1536:def _merge_context(left: Optional[str], right: Optional[str], owner: str, compiler: _Compiler) -> Optional[str]:\n1542:def _literal_value(expr: Expr, where: str) -> Any:\n1550:def _arithmetic(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Any:\n1564:def _compare(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\n1571:def _fold_bool(op: str, left: Any, right: Any) -> Optional[bool]:\n1577:def compile_program(program: Program, bindings: CompileBindings,\n1598:def _load_schema() -> dict[str, Any]:\n1605:def _invalid(code: str, message: str, location: str) -> Diagnostic:\n1609:def _nodes(ir: Mapping[str, Any]) -> tuple[dict[str, tuple[str, Mapping[str, Any]]], Optional[Diagnostic]]:\n1624:def _ref(nodes: Mapping[str, tuple[str, Mapping[str, Any]]], identifier: str,\n1770:def _expression_bounds(identifier, nodes):\n1793:def validate_ir(ir: Mapping[str, Any], bindings: CompileBindings,\n1841:            if row[\"dimensions\"] or row[\"concept\"] != \"debt_principal\" or row[\"measurement\"] != \"principal\" or row[\"time\"][\"calendar\"] != bindings.calendar_id or row[\"perimeter\"] != bindings.entity_perimeter:\n2076:def _validate_profile_integrity(ir, bindings, nodes, checker):\n2148:def evaluate_expression(ir: Mapping[str, Any], identifier: str,\n2201:def semantic_projection(ir: Mapping[str, Any] | None) -> Optional[dict[str, Any]]:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
